      "expected": "A 0 Ω resistor (R10) should be populated in this position to directly connect the selected M5Stack bus pin (PWM1_C2 for Core2/CoreS3) to PWM1, as stated in the specification for R9–R12 jumpers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "C6 100u"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "In PWM mode for Core2/CoreS3, the PWM1_C2 signal cannot drive PWM1 directly. The series 100 µF capacitor blocks DC and differentiates the PWM waveform, so the servo receives no correct control pulses. The intended 0 Ω jumper path is missing.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains one clear anomaly: a 100 µF capacitor (C6) occupies the position intended for the 0 Ω PWM1_C2 jumper (R10), which would prevent proper PWM signal routing for Core2/CoreS3."
}

